<p>Example Goods Ltd wants everyone, including people with disabilities, to be able to use Example Goods. This statement explains the standard we work to, what we have checked, the barriers we know about, and how to contact us.</p>
<p>This statement covers Example Goods at <a href="https://example-goods.example/">https://example-goods.example/</a>.</p>
<h2>Measures we take</h2>
<ul>
<li>We run automated accessibility checks on Example Goods every week.</li>
<li>We fix barriers where they start, in our store data and theme code, and keep a dated record of every fix.</li>
<li>Since September 1, 2026, we have fixed 128 barriers found by these checks, and later scans showed they were gone.</li>
<li>Our staff check new product pages with a keyboard before they go live.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Status against WCAG 2.2 Level AA</h2>
<p>The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, published by the W3C, describe how to make web content more accessible to people with disabilities. We use WCAG 2.2 Level AA as our standard.</p>
<p>Our latest automated checks, on October 16, 2026, found no failures. Automated checks cannot test every WCAG 2.2 Level AA success criterion, so this does not show that Example Goods meets the standard in full. The criteria that need a person to check are listed under How we checked.</p>
<p>In the scan on October 16, 2026, Example Goods passed 310 of 310 automated WCAG 2.2 Level AA checks.</p>
<p>Automated testing finds only part of all accessibility barriers. Deque, the maker of the axe-core engine these checks use, reports that axe-core finds on average 57% of WCAG issues. The rest need a person to check.</p>
<h2>Known limitations</h2>
<p>We do not know of any barriers on Example Goods at the moment. If you find one, please tell us.</p>
<p>Shopify provides the checkout pages, and some features come from third-party apps. We report barriers we find in them to their providers.</p>
<h2>Feedback and contact</h2>
<p>If you find an accessibility barrier on Example Goods, or need information in a different format, please tell us:</p>
<ul>
<li>Email: <a href="mailto:access@example-goods.example">access@example-goods.example</a></li>
<li>Phone: <a href="tel:+15550100199">+1 555 010 0199</a></li>
<li>Post: 1 Example Street, Example City</li>
<li>Online form: <a href="https://example-goods.example/pages/report-a-barrier">report a barrier</a></li>
</ul>
<p>We aim to reply within 5 business days.</p>
<h2>Technical information</h2>
<p>Example Goods relies on HTML, CSS, JavaScript and WAI-ARIA to work with your web browser and any assistive technology you use.</p>
<p>We test with current versions of Chrome, Firefox and Safari.</p>
<h2>How we checked</h2>
<p>We evaluate Example Goods ourselves, with Rampsmith&#39;s automated checks of WCAG 2.2 Level A and AA. The latest scan finished on October 16, 2026 and checked 1 page.</p>
<ul>
<li>Our team tested checkout-free pages with NVDA and VoiceOver. (October 10, 2026)</li>
</ul>
<p>WCAG 2.2 has 55 success criteria at Level A and AA. Each one below is either tested by automated checks, tested only in part, or not tested by automated checks at all.</p>
<h3>Tested by automated checks: 0 criteria</h3>
<p>None.</p>
<h3>Tested in part; a person must check the rest: 1 criterion</h3>
<ul>
<li>1.1.1 Non-text Content (Level A)</li>
</ul>
